Hi! I've been having problems with doing a two-period time stratified model. No matter how I change the connectivity, it always produces NaNs in the relative_probs_of_each_state_at_branch_top_AT_node_DOWNPASS table. I've tried constraining it less and more, and even setting the on_NaN_error term to -1e50 didn't help. I'm trying to pinpoint exactly what nodes/areas are related to the problem, but I think I may be reading the table wrong. Can you tell me what the rows and columns in the relative probabilities table refer to? Thanks.

